content:
I looked for every place we still instantiate the old `generic_sram` cells and found that it’s really just our two memories (the cluster‐L1 scratchpad and the SoC‐L2 banks) plus the upstream generic cell definition itself.  Those three spots are where we need to swap in `tc_sram` (with the right parameters) and then retire the old generic wrapper.

```
// 1) cluster’s on-chip TCDM banks use generic_sram
hw/ip/cluster/src/cluster_tcdm.sv

// 2) the top-level cluster file also instantiates that memory
hw/ip/cluster/src/cluster.sv

// 3) the SoC L2 memory banks likewise use generic_sram
hw/ip/l2/src/memory.sv

// 4) finally, retire/replace the generic_sram cell itself
hw/lib/rtl/generic_sram.sv
```
